{
  "id": "bathhouse",
  "name": "The Bathhouse",
  "description": "An old public bathhouse on Velvet's street under the Cat: cheap by Velvet's standards, where house workers wash off a shift and people from rival houses can sit in the same water without it meaning anything. A tall hall of worn white and blue tiles under dark beams, tall windows on the night sky to the left. A faded tile mural of a moonlit bay with sailing boats covers the back wall, chipped and patched. A wide sunken bath of still water fills the middle, a brass spout pouring into it. Along the left wall, low washing stations with wooden stools and buckets, mirrors and a row of small lamps; paper lanterns hang from the beams. On the right, a drinks vending machine, a little shelf shrine with a candle, and the curtained doorway back through the changing room to the street.",
